":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.5.beta4.mono.official\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS 15.5 (24F74)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using **Quaternion(Vector3 arcFrom, Vector3 arcTo)** in Godot 4.5 mono beta, the value returned is different from 4.4 and it is causing some issues.\n\n**Godot 4.5**\n`var target = new Quaternion(Vector3.Up, Vector3.Up);\n        GD.Print(target); // returns (0, 0, 0, 0)`\n\n**Godot 4.4**\n`var target = new Quaternion(Vector3.Up, Vector3.Up);\n        GD.Print(target); // returns (0, 0, 0, 1)`\n\nApparently this might be something to do with C# having a quaternion default of (0,0,0,0). I don't know a lot about the inner workings of quaternions but this has been causing some issues with the resulting quaternion.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd this to a script in Godot 4.5 beta \n\nvar target = new Quaternion(Vector3.Up, Vector3.Up);\nGD.Print(target);\n\nThe result will be (0, 0, 0, 0)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNot sure an MRP is necessary here. ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"